===============================================================================
TERMINAL POLICY
===============================================================================

Windows PowerShell HTTP Testing

When testing local HTTP endpoints on Windows:

Prefer:

- curl.exe
- Invoke-RestMethod

Avoid using PowerShell's curl alias because it resolves to Invoke-WebRequest
and may display interactive security prompts.

Examples:

- curl.exe http://localhost:3000/api/health
- Invoke-RestMethod http://localhost:3000/api/health

Non-Interactive Terminal Commands

Before executing terminal commands:

- Reuse existing terminal sessions.
- Prefer non-interactive commands suitable for automation.
- Avoid commands that pause waiting for user input.
- Avoid interactive installers when a silent or non-interactive option exists.
- If an interactive command is unavoidable, explain why before executing it.

Development Shell Awareness

Assume Windows PowerShell unless the repository or user explicitly specifies
another shell.

Generate terminal commands compatible with the active shell.

Do not mix PowerShell, CMD, Bash, or WSL syntax in the same instruction unless
explicitly required.

